---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="StudioBooking | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="studiobooking" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/StudioBooking.png" alt="StudioBooking application preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">StudioBooking</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A SaaS booking platform for professionals and studios, built with Laravel and Tailwind CSS, with Claude used as an AI development partner.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>StudioBooking is a software-as-a-service product for appointment scheduling. It is designed for professionals, independent operators, and studios that need a clean way to manage availability, bookings, clients, and service flow.</p>
      <p>The product focuses on the operational side of service businesses: reducing back-and-forth messages, making availability visible, and helping teams organize appointments in one place.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Product concept, Laravel development, Tailwind interface implementation, booking workflow design, application structure, and AI-assisted iteration with Claude.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>Booking software needs to be simple for clients and reliable for the business. The challenge was to define a product structure that can support appointments, services, professionals, and availability without becoming confusing.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Built the product foundation with Laravel for maintainable backend workflows.</li>
        <li>Used Tailwind CSS to create a straightforward interface for booking and management screens.</li>
        <li>Structured the product around services, professionals, availability, and appointment states.</li>
        <li>Used Claude as an AI collaborator to explore implementation paths and refine product flows.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>StudioBooking is positioned as a practical scheduling SaaS for service-based businesses, with a technical foundation that can grow into payments, reminders, client history, and studio-level administration.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
